@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"

Feature: WWW Homepage
	Frontend testing for the www homepage

Scenario: Social Media Footer Navigation
	End users should be able to view all links in the social media section of the footer.

	Given I go to the www homepage
	And I click on the footer "Facebook" social media link
	And I select the window titled "Liferay - Home | Facebook"
	Then there should be no errors on the page
	When I close the window titled "Liferay - Home | Facebook"
	And I click on the footer "Github" social media link
	And I select the window titled "Liferay Inc. · GitHub"
	Then there should be no errors on the page
	When I close the window titled "Liferay Inc. · GitHub"
	And I click on the footer "Instagram" social media link
	And I select the window titled "Liferay, Inc. (@liferayinc) • Instagram photos and videos"
	Then there should be no errors on the page
	When I close the window titled "Liferay, Inc. (@liferayinc) • Instagram photos and videos"
	And I click on the footer "LinkedIn" social media link
	And I select the pop up window
	Then there should be no errors on the page
	When I close the pop up window
	And I click on the footer "Twitter" social media link
	And I select the window titled "Liferay (@Liferay) / Twitter"
	Then there should be no errors on the page
	When I close the window titled "Liferay (@Liferay) / Twitter"
	And I click on the footer "YouTube" social media link
	And I select the window titled "Liferay - YouTube"
	Then there should be no errors on the page
	And I close the window titled "Liferay - YouTube"

Scenario: Additional Footer Navigation
	End users should be able to view additional links in the footer.

	Given I go to the www homepage
	And I click on the footer "Contact us" link
	Then there should be no errors on the page
	And the current url content should contain the text "www-uat.liferay.com"
	When I go to the www homepage
	And I click on the footer "Privacy Policy" link
	Then there should be no errors on the page
	And the current url content should contain the text "www-uat.liferay.com"

Scenario: Change Languages
	End users should be able to change all languages in the site.

	Given I go to the www homepage
	And I change the language of the site to "Chinese"
	Then there should be no errors on the page
	And the current url content should contain the text "/zh"
	When I go to the translated www homepage
	And I change the language of the site to "Australian English"
	Then there should be no errors on the page
	And the current url content should contain the text "/en-AU"
	When I go to the translated www homepage
	And I change the language of the site to "American English"
	Then there should be no errors on the page
	When I go to the www homepage
	And I change the language of the site to "French"
	Then there should be no errors on the page
	And the current url content should contain the text "/fr"
	When I go to the translated www homepage
	And I change the language of the site to "German"
	Then there should be no errors on the page
	And the current url content should contain the text "/de"
	When I go to the translated www homepage
	And I change the language of the site to "Italian"
	Then there should be no errors on the page
	And the current url content should contain the text "/it"
	When I go to the translated www homepage
	And I change the language of the site to "Portuguese"
	Then there should be no errors on the page
	And the current url content should contain the text "/pt"
	When I go to the translated www homepage
	And I change the language of the site to "Spanish"
	Then there should be no errors on the page
	And the current url content should contain the text "/es"
	When I go to the translated www homepage
	And I change the language of the site to "Japanese"
	Then there should be no errors on the page
	And the current url content should contain the text ".co.jp"

Scenario: Change languages via footer dropdown
	End users should be able to change all languages in the site via footer language dropdown.

	Given I go to the www homepage
	And I change the language of the site to "中文" via footer dropdown
	Then there should be no errors on the page
	And the current url content should contain the text "/zh"
	When I go to the translated www homepage
	And I change the language of the site to "English (Australia)" via footer dropdown
	Then there should be no errors on the page
	And the current url content should contain the text "/en-AU"
	When I go to the translated www homepage
	And I change the language of the site to "English (United States)" via footer dropdown
	Then there should be no errors on the page
	When I go to the www homepage
	And I change the language of the site to "Français" via footer dropdown
	Then there should be no errors on the page
	And the current url content should contain the text "/fr"
	When I go to the translated www homepage
	And I change the language of the site to "Deutsch" via footer dropdown
	Then there should be no errors on the page
	And the current url content should contain the text "/de"
	When I go to the translated www homepage
	And I change the language of the site to "Italiano" via footer dropdown
	Then there should be no errors on the page
	And the current url content should contain the text "/it"
	When I go to the translated www homepage
	And I change the language of the site to "Português" via footer dropdown
	Then there should be no errors on the page
	And the current url content should contain the text "/pt"
	When I go to the translated www homepage
	And I change the language of the site to "Español" via footer dropdown
	Then there should be no errors on the page
	And the current url content should contain the text "/es"
	When I go to the translated www homepage
	And I change the language of the site to "日本語" via footer dropdown
	Then there should be no errors on the page
	And the current url content should contain the text ".co.jp"

Scenario: View homepage title and meta description
	The homepage title and meta description should be specific values.

	Given I go to the www homepage
	Then the current page title should be "Digital Experience Software Tailored to Your Needs | Liferay"
	And the current page meta description should be "Build portals, intranets, websites and connected experiences on the most extensible digital experience platform around. Learn more."

Scenario: View OG Tags
	The homepage og tags should be specific values.

	Given I go to the www homepage
	Then the current page og title tag should be "Digital Experience Software Tailored to Your Needs | Liferay"
	And the current page og description tag should be "Build portals, intranets, websites and connected experiences on the most extensible digital experience platform around. Learn more."
	And the current page og url tag should be "https://www-uat.liferay.com/"
	And the current page og image tag should be "https://www-uat.liferay.com/documents/10182/0/open_graph_image+%281%29.png/a608e357-83f6-e392-979c-6599a8618634?version=1.0&t=1646949040894&imagePreview=1"

Scenario: View homepage hreflang tags
	All hreflang tags on the homepage should be specific values.

	Given I go to the www homepage
	Then the hreflang tag for the relative language url "zh/" should be "zh-CN"
	And the hreflang tag for the relative language url "es/" should be "es-ES"
	And the hreflang tag for the relative language url "it/" should be "it-IT"
	And the hreflang tag for the relative language url "fr/" should be "fr-FR"
	And the hreflang tag for the relative language url "" should be "en-US"
	And the hreflang tag for the relative language url "pt/" should be "pt-BR"
	And the hreflang tag for the relative language url "de/" should be "de-DE"

Scenario: View homepage hreflang canonical tags
	Correct hreflang canonical tags should be present upon language changes.

	Given I go to the www homepage
	And I change the language of the site to "Chinese"
	Then the hreflang canonical tag for the relative language url "zh/" should be present
	When I go to the translated www homepage
	And I change the language of the site to "American English"
	Then the hreflang canonical tag for the relative language url "" should be present
	When I go to the www homepage
	And I change the language of the site to "French"
	Then the hreflang canonical tag for the relative language url "fr/" should be present
	When I go to the translated www homepage
	And I change the language of the site to "German"
	Then the hreflang canonical tag for the relative language url "de/" should be present
	When I go to the translated www homepage
	And I change the language of the site to "Italian"
	Then the hreflang canonical tag for the relative language url "it/" should be present
	When I go to the translated www homepage
	And I change the language of the site to "Portuguese"
	Then the hreflang canonical tag for the relative language url "pt/" should be present
	When I go to the translated www homepage
	And I change the language of the site to "Spanish"
	Then the hreflang canonical tag for the relative language url "es/" should be present